    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `build_server()` in `app/server.py`. The server is named \"notes\", both tools work, and `python -m app.server` still serves over stdio.\n\n**About mcp 2.2.0:** the SDK no longer has `FastMCP`. The high-level decorator API is now `MCPServer` in `mcp.server.mcpserver`, and tools are registered with `@server.tool()`.\n\n**The unknown-title error:** `word_count` raises `ToolError(f\"no such note: {title}\")`, which the model receives as a tool error it can read. This had to be `ToolError` specifically. In 2.2.0, any other exception, such as `KeyError` or `ValueError`, is treated as a crash, and the model only sees `Error executing tool word_count` without the reason.\n\n**Checks run:**\n- `pytest -q`: 1 passed.\n- `python -m app.smoke` lists `add_note` and `word_count`.\n- I also called the tools over stdio with a separate script:\n  - `add_note(\"a\", \"one two  three\\nfour\")` returned `saved a`.\n  - `word_count(\"a\")` returned `4`.\n  - `word_count(\"zz\")` came back as a tool error with the text `Error executing tool word_count: no such note: zz`.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** I couldn't delete that test script, `_e2e_check.py`, from the project root because the delete needs your approval. It isn't needed anymore, so please remove it (`rm _e2e_check.py`).\n\nNo dependencies were added or changed."
